<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">British New Guinea</h1><p class="st-meta">1884 CE – 1906 CE · capital Port Moresby</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British protectorate and then colony in southeastern New Guinea, administered for the Australian colonies and handed to Australia as Papua.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Fearing German expansion, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-queensland">Queensland</a> tried to annex eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> in 1883, but <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> disallowed the move. In November 1884 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-elphinstone-erskine">Commodore James Erskine</a> proclaimed a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the southeast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-moresby">Port Moresby</a>, days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> had raised its flag over the north, which became <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-new-guinea">German New Guinea</a>. In 1888 the territory was annexed as a crown colony.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was funded largely by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-queensland">Queensland</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-new-south-wales">New South Wales</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-victoria">Victoria</a>. Administrator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-macgregor">William MacGregor</a>, from 1888 to 1898, explored the interior, set up government stations, appointed village constables and restricted land sales to Europeans. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> workers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-chalmers-missionary">James Chalmers</a>, who was killed in 1901, were influential along the coast. Small gold rushes on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/misima">Misima</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodlark-island">Woodlark Island</a> drew prospectors.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After federation, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> transferred the colony to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-act-1905">Papua Act</a> of 1905, which took effect in 1906, when it was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/territory-of-papua">Territory of Papua</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-macgregor">MacGregor</a>'s network of government stations and village constables remained the basis of Australian administration.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/british-new-guinea.jpg" alt="British New Guinea" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: vectored by FOX 52 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_British_New_Guinea_(1888%E2%80%931906).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1884 CE – 1906 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port Moresby</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William MacGregor, Peter Scratchley</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous religions, Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Motu, Papuan and Austronesian languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Protectorate of British New Guinea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1895&amp;focus=british-new-guinea" aria-label="British New Guinea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8741 2531 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where British New Guinea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9061 2787L4997 651M9061 2787L9061 2787"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M9061 2787h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9061 2787h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9061 2787h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Port Moresby. <a href="/atlas?year=1895&amp;focus=british-new-guinea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
